 {
  "title": "Show HN: Tinnitus frequency finder and audio notch tool",
  "url": "https://trynotched.com/find",
  "author": "brianrhea",
  "points": 182,
  "story_text": "I&#x27;ve had tinnitus for about a year and a half. There&#x27;s no cure, so I&#x27;m trying anything that looks promising. One idea people are researching is listening to sound with a notch cut out right at your tinnitus frequency.<p>The frequency finder will help you zero in on your tinnitus pitch. The method write-up is here: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;trynotched.com&#x2F;how-pitch-matching-works\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;trynotched.com&#x2F;how-pitch-matching-works</a><p>Once you have a pitch, there&#x27;s a free web app that plays background sounds (stream, rain, wind and so on) with a notch at your frequency: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;trynotched.com&#x2F;tools\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;trynotched.com&#x2F;tools</a>.<p>I built it as a PWA so you can save to your phone&#x27;s home screen and it works offline. No account or time limit.",
